<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-5551] Zeppelin does not support JDBC interpreter for trino v358 and above</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-5551</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;1. prestosql has been renamed to trino since 2020.12&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://trino.io/blog/2020/12/27/announcing-trino.html&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://trino.io/blog/2020/12/27/announcing-trino.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&#160;2. jdbc interpreter supports only `com.facebook.presto.jdbc.PrestoDriver` and `io.prestosql.jdbc.PrestoDriver` after bug (check issue below)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/blob/v0.10.0/jdbc/src/main/java/org/apache/zeppelin/jdbc/JDBCInterpreter.java#L476-L485&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/blob/v0.10.0/jdbc/src/main/java/org/apache/zeppelin/jdbc/JDBCInterpreter.java#L476-L485&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-2891&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-2891&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;3. trino no longer supports the name `io.prestosql.jdbc.PrestoDriver` and has been removed in v358.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/trinodb/trino/commit/86136cea9b6d525a830c3eb70a3db937b947e257&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;- https://github.com/trinodb/trino/commit/86136cea9b6d525a830c3eb70a3db937b947e257&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;4. For backward compatible, need to add trino driver name to support v358 and above&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
