                            <comment id="17471374" author="orin" created="Sun, 9 Jan 2022 15:19:33 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I&apos;m trying to configure an interpreter manually on the v0.1 (docker image) but I get the following exception:&lt;br/&gt;
java.sql.SQLException: Unrecognized connection property &apos;url&apos;&lt;br/&gt;
at io.trino.jdbc.TrinoDriverUri.validateConnectionProperties(TrinoDriverUri.java:472)&lt;br/&gt;
Can someone help?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I thought I could replace the&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;/opt/zeppelin/interpreter/jdbc/zeppelin-jdbc-0.10.0.jar with its newer version as a workaround. Do you think it will work? I saw the version inside the docker container is 3MB while the version in maven is 58k, probably because of dependencies&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17471621" author="jyoo94" created="Mon, 10 Jan 2022 00:20:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=orin&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;orin&quot;&gt;orin&lt;/a&gt;&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
what version of trino/jdbc are you using? debug or checkout the code if config is set up properly.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/trinodb/trino/blob/master/client/trino-jdbc/src/main/java/io/trino/jdbc/TrinoDriverUri.java#L472&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/trinodb/trino/blob/master/client/trino-jdbc/src/main/java/io/trino/jdbc/TrinoDriverUri.java#L472&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17471685" author="orin" created="Mon, 10 Jan 2022 06:33:20 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This is what I did to apply the fix on a my container:&lt;br/&gt;
1. Start a new container to build the jdbc jar - used maven image with open-jdk java 1.8:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
docker run -it --rm --name my-java --mount type=bind,source=&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;$(pwd)&quot;&lt;/span&gt;/output,target=/output maven:3-openjdk-8 /bin/bash &lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;2. Inside the container build the jdbc jar, the new jar - which will be placed in the current dir of the host:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
git clone https:&lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;//github.com/apache/zeppelin.git
&lt;/span&gt;cd zeppelin
mvn --projects zeppelin-common,zeppelin-interpreter,zeppelin-interpreter-shaded,jdbc clean &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;package&lt;/span&gt; -DskipTestscp 
cp interpreter/jdbc/zeppelin-jdbc-0.11.0-SNAPSHOT.jar /output/ &lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;3. Replace the jar in the zeppelin container. The target name is for the latest docker image:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
docker cp zeppelin-jdbc-0.11.0-SNAPSHOT.jar your-container-name:/opt/zeppelin/interpreter/jdbc/zeppelin-jdbc-0.10.0.jar &lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
